# Lines make check-serial (and tools/pi-run, live) must see on the Pi 5, in
# this order, as whole serial lines: rpi5b_2gb/usb-stream-test.system, the
# Pi 5 only. Each USB host PD
# runs its controller as usb-test's do; what is plugged in, on which port,
# differs by desk and is printed between these lines, not checked here -
# the run's log shows each stream's 10 s reports, "600 s, no interval
# missed" among them. The run ends at its run length, 660 s (the ticker's
# last line). A missed interval anywhere in the run fails it, as a stream
# not streamed does.
NOWAYOS: usb0: starting
NOWAYOS: usb0: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb0: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb0: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb0: ready
NOWAYOS: usb1: starting
NOWAYOS: usb1: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb1: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb1: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb1: ready
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: the run length is reached: no more ticks, so the watchdog services no more and the board resets

# Output that fails the run at once if it appears anywhere (substring match).
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!could not service
!not streamed
!missed so far
